Unknown option: -x

Usage:
    convert-comics [options] <inputDir> <outputDir>

Converts every comic book under <inputDir> into a .cbz of AVIF pages in the
mirrored folder under <outputDir>. Books may be .cbr/.cbz/.cb7 archives or PDFs
that hold one large image per page; a PDF that is not shaped like a scanned comic
(a magazine, a text document) is reported and skipped.

Options:
    -h, --help      Print this help page.
    -l, --quality <quality>
                    quality level of the output images, default 45
    -u, --chroma <chroma>
                    page chroma: 420 or 444. 444 keeps colour at full resolution,
                    420 at a quarter of it, for smaller books with colour
                    fringes on thin lines and lettering. Default 444.
    -s, --speed <speed>
                    av1 speed preset, lower is slower, default 4
    -m, --max-resolution <maxRes>
                    maximum resolution (height) to keep, default 2960
    -f, --fuzz <fuzz>
                    when trimming, how many percent color difference gets still
                    trimmed, default 10
    -v, --verbose   Also say why each item was handled the way it was, and on a
                    failure print the tool's whole output rather than its last
                    lines.
    -q, --quiet     Print errors only - no progress and no warnings.

Nothing was changed.
